Files that must NOT be uploaded as static assets.
_worker.js is our Worker entry point (referenced by main in
wrangler.toml). Wrangler's static-asset bundler sees the filename and
refuses to proceed without an explicit opt-out, since uploading the
file would expose server-side code at https://<site>/_worker.js.
_worker.js

Wrangler's own config — not for public serving.
wrangler.toml

The bat file is a dev convenience; nothing on the site references it.
deploy.bat

Local Durable Object state and Wrangler cache. Contains binary data
from local dev runs and should never leave the developer machine.
.wrangler/

If you ever add one.
node_modules/

Git internals, in case someone deploys from a checkout that hasn't
been cleaned.
.git/
.gitignore